{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"boundary","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Repository configuration can execute a command with factory privileges during delivery or land-queue pushes when those settings are planted."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"outage","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An ordinary local Git identity causes manual landing to stop before checks run."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"test","trigger":"plausible","reason":"On a busy or slower machine, the integration tests can exceed their default timeout despite succeeding with a larger budget."},{"id":"C4","consequence":"boundary","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A background process can change repository configuration after validation and cause the subsequent push to execute a command with the script's privileges."},{"id":"C5","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A credential embedded in a URL-scoped Git configuration key is printed to stderr and potentially captured in logs."},{"id":"C1b","consequence":"boundary","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A planted URL rewrite and transport setting can execute a command with factory privileges during delivery or land-queue pushes."}]}